x", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 59230, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_019NLRXxSA5LPYqrJvgcupzx", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 59230, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_019NLRXxSA5LPYqrJvgcupzx", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 65359, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, its most recent healthy release, in all three regions, and the service is passing health checks again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Before:** every region was on v2.3.1, which was failing health checks with an 18% error rate. v2.3.1-rc had also failed in production.\n- **First attempt:** this stopped partway. An orchestrator error halted the rollout after us-east, so us-east was on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1. Since v2.3.0 is a known-healthy version, I ran the rollback again.\n- **Second attempt:** this finished in all regions. us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0, healthy, with a 0.2% error rate.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created anyway, so I didn't retry. There's one incident and one page, not two.\n- INC-0001 describes the failure, the stalled first rollback, the current state and two follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed before anyone redeploys it.\n  - Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01KU6Mxzan4v2cTQhKr7aHYP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type