 stopped the rollout after us-east, leaving the regions on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0; us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). A second rollback finished in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west. The service is healthy with a 0.2% error rate. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying it, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so it may have been created anyway. I'll check before retrying so I don't page twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_019NLRXxSA5LPYqrJvgcupzx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, its most recent healthy release, in all three regions, and the service is passing health checks again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Before:** every region was on v2.3.1, which was failing health checks with an 18% error rate. v2.3.1-rc had also failed in production.\n- **First attempt:** this stopped partway. An orchestrator error halted the rollout after us-east, so us-east was on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1. Since v2.3.0 is a known-healthy version, I ran the rollback again.\n- **Second attempt:** this finished in all regions. us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0, healthy, with a 0.2% error rate.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created anyway, so I didn't retry. There's one incident and one page, not two.\n- INC-0001 describes the failure, the stalled first rollback, the current state and two follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed before anyone redeploys it.\n  - Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}